                    <mutableString key="text">Carmie (“Carmie,” “we,” “our,” or “us”) respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, disclose, and protect your information when you use the Carmie mobile application and related services.

Carmie is available globally except in Mainland China.

By using Carmie, you agree to the collection and use of information described in this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, please do not use Carmie.

1. Information We Collect

We may collect the following types of information when you use Carmie.

1.1 Account Information

When you create or manage an account, we may collect:

Username or display name;
Email address;
Profile photo or avatar;
Account login information;
User preferences and profile settings.
1.2 User Content

We may collect content that you create, upload, post, share, send, or display through Carmie, including:

Short videos;
Gesture and dance content;
Comments;
Messages;
Remix or challenge participation content;
Profile descriptions;
Images, audio, and other materials you choose to upload.

You are responsible for ensuring that your User Content does not include private, sensitive, illegal, or unauthorized information belonging to others.

1.3 Video Call and Communication Information

If you use Carmie’s video call, chat, comment, or interaction features, we may process information related to those communications, such as:

Call participation information;
Interaction history;
Messages and comments;
Reports, moderation records, or safety-related information.

We may review communication-related information when necessary to enforce our User Agreement, protect users, prevent abuse, or comply with legal obligations.

1.4 AI Feature Information

Carmie may provide AI tools that recommend gesture combinations, choreography ideas, expression suggestions, or creative prompts.

When you use AI features, we may collect:

Inputs you provide to AI tools;
AI-generated suggestions shown to you;
Your interactions with AI recommendations;
Feedback or usage patterns related to AI features.

We use this information to provide, improve, personalize, and maintain the safety of Carmie’s AI features.

1.5 Device and Technical Information

We may automatically collect technical information, including:

Device model and operating system;
App version;
IP address;
Device identifiers;
Language and region settings;
Network information;
Crash logs;
Performance data;
Usage logs and diagnostic information.
1.6 Usage Information

We may collect information about how you use Carmie, such as:

Videos viewed, liked, shared, or remixed;
Challenges joined;
Gesture guides or expression guides viewed;
Search activity within the app;
Features used;
Time spent in the app;
Interactions with other users.
1.7 Location Information

We may infer your general location from your IP address, such as country or region, for purposes such as app availability, safety, analytics, and legal compliance.

We do not collect precise GPS location unless we ask for your permission and you choose to provide it.

2. How We Use Your Information

We may use your information to:

Provide, operate, maintain, and improve Carmie;
Create and manage your account;
Enable video sharing, remixing, comments, chats, and video calls;
Recommend videos, gestures, challenges, choreography ideas, and AI-assisted creative suggestions;
Personalize your experience;
Moderate content and enforce our User Agreement;
Detect, prevent, and respond to fraud, spam, abuse, security incidents, and illegal activity;
Analyze app performance and user engagement;
Fix bugs and improve app functionality;
Communicate with you about service updates, security alerts, and support requests;
Comply with applicable laws, regulations, and legal processes.
3. How We Share Your Information

We do not sell your personal information.

We may share information in the following circumstances:

3.1 With Other Users

Some information may be visible to other users, including:

Your username;
Profile photo;
Public videos;
Comments;
Remix or challenge participation content;
Public interactions;
Other information you choose to make public.

Please be careful when sharing information publicly.

3.2 With Service Providers

We may share information with trusted third-party service providers that help us operate Carmie, such as:

Cloud hosting providers;
Analytics providers;
Content moderation tools;
Customer support tools;
Security and anti-fraud providers;
AI technology service providers;
Video call or communication service providers.

These providers may only process your information as needed to provide services to us.

3.3 For Legal and Safety Reasons

We may disclose information if we believe it is necessary to:

Comply with applicable law, regulation, legal process, or government request;
Enforce our User Agreement or other policies;
Protect the rights, safety, and property of Carmie, users, or others;
Detect or prevent fraud, abuse, security threats, or illegal activity;
Respond to emergencies.
3.4 Business Transfers

If Carmie is involved in a merger, acquisition, financing, restructuring, sale of assets, or similar transaction, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction.

4. User Content and Public Visibility

Carmie is a social app. Content you post publicly may be viewed, shared, remixed, commented on, or interacted with by other users.

Depending on app features and your settings, other users may be able to see:

Your public profile;
Videos you upload;
Challenges you join;
Comments you post;
Public interactions;
Remix content based on your posts.

Do not post content that you do not want others to see, save, copy, share, or remix.

5. AI Features and Personalization

Carmie may use AI-powered tools to suggest gesture combinations, choreography ideas, expression styles, creative prompts, or content recommendations.

AI outputs are generated based on available inputs and system design. They may not always be accurate, appropriate, original, or suitable for every user.

We may use your interactions with AI features to improve recommendations, safety, quality, and user experience.

You must not use AI features to create or promote illegal, harmful, infringing, abusive, sexual, exploitative, violent, discriminatory, or otherwise prohibited content.

6. Cookies and Similar Technologies

Carmie or its service providers may use cookies, local storage, SDKs, pixels, or similar technologies to:

Keep you logged in;
Remember your preferences;
Analyze app usage;
Improve performance;
Prevent fraud and abuse;
Provide personalized content and recommendations.

You may be able to control certain tracking technologies through your device settings.

7. Data Retention

We retain your information for as long as necessary to provide Carmie, maintain your account, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, enforce agreements, protect safety, and improve our services.

If you delete your account or request deletion of your information, we will take reasonable steps to delete or anonymize your personal information, unless we need to retain it for legal, security, safety, or legitimate business reasons.

Some content may remain visible if it has been shared, remixed, copied, or stored by other users before deletion.

8. Data Security

We use reasonable technical, organizational, and administrative measures to protect your information from unauthorized access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure.

However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security of your information.

9. Your Rights and Choices

Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights to:

Access the personal information we hold about you;
Correct inaccurate information;
Delete your account or personal information;
Object to or restrict certain processing;
Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent;
Request a copy of your information;
Opt out of certain communications or personalized features.

To make a privacy request, contact us at carmie@gmail.com
.

We may need to verify your identity before processing certain requests.

10. Children’s Privacy

Carmie is not intended for children under the minimum age required by applicable law.

Users who are under the age of majority in their country or region should use Carmie only with permission from a parent or legal guardian.

We do not knowingly collect personal information from children where prohibited by law. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information without proper consent, please contact us at carmie@gmail.com
, and we will take appropriate action.

11. International Data Transfers

Carmie is available globally except in Mainland China. Your information may be processed and stored in countries or regions outside your place of residence.

These countries may have different data protection laws from your country or region. Where required, we will take appropriate measures to protect your information in accordance with applicable law.

12. Third-Party Links and Services

Carmie may contain links to third-party websites, services, music, content, or integrations.

This Privacy Policy does not apply to third-party services. We are not responsible for the privacy practices, content, or policies of third parties. Please review their privacy policies before using them.

13. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we may notify you through the app or by other reasonable means.

Your continued use of Carmie after the updated Privacy Policy becomes effective means you accept the updated policy.

14. Contact Us

If you have any questions, requests, or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:

Email: carmie@gmail.com</mutableString>
